on with no single-q tail. E.g., a geodesic that escapes to i0 or has a tail approaching a horizon generator... Constructing a rigorous example is hard; but one can give a heuristic/structural argument. Hmm, that could be a legit class-bound falsifier task but risks overreach (physics).

